data check_subject_shape_cannot_represent_the_state_the_check_detects: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "check_subject_shape_cannot_represent_the_state_the_check_detects" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a lens is correct and live over a subject shape that cannot represent the state it detects** (a check reaches its subject, executes on every run, and is enrolled as coverage -- and its RED is UNAUTHORABLE there, because the representation the subject is expressed in has no constructor for the state the check matches on. Nothing is skipped, nothing is absorbed, no population is withheld, and the check is not wrong: hand it a value of the shape it expects and it fires correctly. It is the SUBJECT that cannot carry the state, so the check is permanently green over that subject while reading as verified. ",
    "**THE BOUNDARY AGAINST check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim DECIDES THE REMEDY AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME DEFECT.** There the subject is a SMALLER POPULATION than the claim -- widen it and the missing instances appear, so the repair is a scope edit. Here the population is exactly right and every member is structurally incapable of exhibiting the state; widening adds more members that equally cannot exhibit it, so a scope edit is guaranteed to change nothing while looking like a fix. It is also NOT absorbing_fallback: nothing widens on failure and no arm degrades -- the check runs its ordinary path to an honest verdict over a subject that could only ever produce one answer. ",
    "**SPECIMEN WITH A RECEIPT, measured 2026-09-03 on gunbc#10245 against origin/main 8b2323f414 and reproduced on 8bfae78d78.** v2.lens.determinism classifies a call through node_callee_symbol, which requires node_is_call, which matches ComputationNode { behavior: Transform }. Its live subject is the fn-arrow body skeletons built by v1_compiler.coproduct_reflection marshal_skeleton, which returns conj_record at both return sites, i.e. TypeNode { connective: Conj }, for EVERY node. A Conj TypeNode cannot satisfy that match, so no skeleton node is ever a call, every body classifies Deterministic by non-membership, and determinism_transitive_holds over a fn_arrow_decl_facts_live population is green by construction. The same mismatch holds four production_qualification_origin_probe_witness frontier rows red, which is what makes it a class rather than an incident: one representation mismatch darkens every consumer of that subject at once. ",
    "**WHY IT SURVIVES REVIEW, and this is the dangerous part.** The check is real, the lens is correct, the subject is live and non-empty, and a positive control asserting the population is non-empty PASSES -- so every ordinary vacuity guard agrees. A NON-EMPTY SUBJECT IS A NECESSARY PRECONDITION MASQUERADING AS THE CHECK. Nine approving reviews passed over the specimen and none exercised the body skeletons; it was found by planting a violation and watching nothing happen. ",
    "**THE BOUNDARY AGAINST live_argument_threaded_past_the_arm_that_decides, filed the same day and easy to conflate with this.** There the check CAN go red -- a different, hand-authored argument decides the verdict and the live argument is threaded past it, so the row is inert with respect to the tree while the predicate itself still discriminates. Here NO argument can produce the refused state, because the subject's representation cannot express it; there is no other arm carrying the verdict, and substituting inputs changes nothing. The two are distinguished by one question: is there an arm that could produce the asserted outcome alone? If yes and the live input is not one of its inputs, that is the threaded-argument class and the remedy is to delete or re-source the row. If no arm can produce the refused outcome at all, this is the class and the remedy is a representation change, which is why its trigger names a shape rather than a call site. ",
    "**RECOGNITION RULE, which is DESIGN 4b's own question asked BEFORE the check is written rather than after: name the state the check refuses, then construct a value in the subject's OWN representation that exhibits it.** If you cannot construct one, the check is a decoration over that subject however correct its logic. The construction is cheap and is the whole test: two values differing only in the field the check keys on, asserting it FIRES on one and is BLIND to the other. Both arms passing is the executing record of the gap; when the representation lands, the blind arm reds and names itself. ",
    "**THE REPORTING RULE THAT FOLLOWS: a class's rung is the minimum across its in-scope paths (4b(1)), so a fixture path where the RED is authorable does NOT stand in for a live path where it is not.** Citing the fixture rung while the live path is dark is rung inflation. **AND IT IS NOT A 4b(3) DECLARED DROP -- filing one is its own error**, which is where the specimen nearly went: 4b(3) governs a REGRESSION, with a previous rung and a population that LOST a guarantee. When the shape mismatch predates the check, the wall was never lit through that path, and a capability that was never real cannot be dropped. The honest instruments are 4b(1) rung honesty and 4b(2) an untracked stall made tracked. ",
    "**RUNG: 1 (mitigatable) -- the gap is nameable and, once found, held open by the two-arm control. CEILING: 4, since whether a subject's representation can inhabit the state a check matches on is decidable from two declarations the tree already carries. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a CAPABILITY and not an artifact: a check declares the subject representation it matches over, and a check whose match is unsatisfiable by that representation fails to compile -- so the decoration cannot be authored at all, rather than being found later by someone constructing the value by hand.**)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
